  "question": {
    "text": "Let the variable line <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></math> is tangent to the hyperbola <math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If the locus of <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a conic, then which of the following statement is false about this conic?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "uA6Qq",
      "text": "Vertices of conic lies on y-axis",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KkeUU",
      "text": "The eccentricity of conic is greater than the eccentricity of given hyperbola.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2n5o5",
      "text": "The centre of conic is at the origin",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PGRj6",
      "text": "The conic is an ellipse",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Equation of the tangent <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;is compared with&nbsp;<math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></msqrt></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></msqrt></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac></math><br />i.e.&nbsp;<math><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></math> and <math><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></msqrt></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></msqrt></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mtext>y</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mtext>x</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mtext>e</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mtext>e</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the conic is not an ellipse</p>",
    "image": null
  },
